                        "sense_id": "0ad745f3-1985-30dc-b8c2-b464f06dc897",
                        "entry_id": "7aec7fb5-a969-30f6-83fb-2427ecf1b1e0",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Overpriced, characteristic of the top of a market."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "of an asset or assets in general"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "8bc9365a-78bb-4fe9-a88a-a78143ed55be",
                                "sense_id": "0ad745f3-1985-30dc-b8c2-b464f06dc897",
                                "text": "[…] because of the vast over-extension of credit, inflation, a generally \"toppy\" condition and a speculative mania in both this country and Europe […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0d08345e-ff57-49b8-8977-f60ec66af9bf",
                                "sense_id": "0ad745f3-1985-30dc-b8c2-b464f06dc897",
                                "text": "The average price of an acre of Iowa farmland ratcheted geometrically from $480 in 1970 to $834 in 1974 to a toppy $2147 in 1981."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "1b2afad0-ff62-4c01-95f3-26fd81b5fc1f",
                                "sense_id": "0ad745f3-1985-30dc-b8c2-b464f06dc897",
                                "text": "Inside GE, Michael Pralle, the man who ran the real estate business and built it into a multibillion-dollar colossus, with Jeff's prodding, knew that the real estate business was getting very toppy."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e08abebe-ea8f-4635-b239-e81b159ef01d",
                                "sense_id": "0ad745f3-1985-30dc-b8c2-b464f06dc897",
                                "text": "Let’s face it, folks: the markets are toppy right now. Yet no one’s officially calling a recession or suggesting what to do if one appears. This is where signals really matter."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "39576a95-fe58-353a-9bdb-7a863b6d6ab9",
                        "entry_id": "7aec7fb5-a969-30f6-83fb-2427ecf1b1e0",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Crazy; mad."
                        ],
